 This install applies to "Powerdrome" (c) 1989 Electronic Arts.
 Supported version: PAL original release.

 Original install by Galahad/Fairlight.
 Version 2.0b enhancements by Vesuri.

 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 18.0 or later and DIC in the path.
 These programs can be found in the WHDLoad package.
 Version 2.0b has been tested with WHDLoad 20.0.
 To install from a different drive than DF0: select installation mode Expert.

 The installed program requires 512 KiB ChipMem and 384 KiB additional memory.
 Extra memory is needed for WHDLoad itself and the optional PRELOAD tooltype.
 Enhanced framerate requires a 68020 or faster CPU and usable Fast RAM.
 It can be quit by pressing F10 (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 The game requires an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image.
 The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts" and
 must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from an A500 with
 tools like 'GrabKick' or similar which can be found on Aminet.
 If the image is the wrong version or altered in any way, WHDLoad will quit
 with an appropriate message.
 Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
 directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive
 "util/boot/skick346.lha" on Aminet.

 Features:
 ---------
 - Full loading from hard disk.
 - Copylock protection removed.
 - EndCLI startup bug removed; the game starts without an extra icon click.
 - Quit option (F10).
 - Manual and hints included.
 - Optional Enhanced framerate mode for 68020+ with Fast RAM.

 Enhanced framerate:
 -------------------
 The installed game icon has the tooltype CUSTOM1=1, so Enhanced framerate is
 ON. Set CUSTOM1=0 in the icon, or untick "Enhanced framerate" in the WHDLoad
 splash screen, for the original rendering and timing. Without the tooltype
 the option is off.

 On a 68020 or faster CPU with usable Fast RAM, it enables:
 - Faster rendering of the original planar graphics in Fast RAM, followed by
   a copy to the Chip RAM display buffer.
 - Fine mouse rotation at 50 updates per second, retaining calibration gain.
 - Fixed-step gameplay timing, so movement and other gameplay updates no
   longer advance once per rendered frame. Cockpit liftoff is paced as well.

 With the option off, on a 68000/68010, or without usable Fast RAM, the game
 retains its original rendering and frame-dependent timing.
 The option does not change WHDLoad's cache policy. CACHE and DCACHE remain
 standard WHDLoad tooltypes under the user's control.

 The timing changes support PAL. Menus, the external pit animation and the
 title demo retain their original timing. NTSC support is not provided.

 Extra notes:
 ------------
 Galahad's original observation still applies:
 "This game is so hard, its unreal! I remember playing this the first time
 around, and it doesn't get any easier!!!"

 Thanks to Slinka & Yoyo for the PAL image.
 Thanks to Frank for the installer and icons.

 History:
 --------
 version 2.0b (09.11.2026) done by Vesuri:
 - Updated the installer to the WHDLoad 20.0 template, retaining the original
   single-disk imaging settings, documentation and icon choices.
 - Reworked the slave using the WHDLoad KickEmu support from version 20.0.
 - Added the single Enhanced framerate option (CUSTOM1=1), set in the
   installed icon; the slave defaults to off.
 - Added Fast RAM planar rendering and static polygon drawing loops.
 - Overlapped Fast RAM rendering with display synchronization and added a
   block copy to publish the completed scene to Chip RAM.
 - Added 20 ms movement steps and 90 ms control updates, with elapsed-time
   handling for input, opponents, resources, repairs, laps and weather.
 - Paced cockpit liftoff to the measured original A500 movement cadence.
 - Added fractional mouse steering with smooth 20 ms rotation updates.
 - Kept original rendering and timing on 68000/68010 and without Fast RAM.
 - Corrected the command-line arguments passed to the game at startup.
 - Retained user control of WHDLoad CACHE and DCACHE options.

 version 1.0 (22.05.2003) done by Galahad/Fairlight:
 - Initial release.
 - Hard disk loading, Copylock removal and EndCLI startup fix.
 - F10 quit option; manual and hints included.
 - Installer and icons by Frank; PAL image supplied by Slinka & Yoyo.

 Contact:
 --------
 If you have problems with this installation, first try the latest version
 of this package from the WHDLoad WWW page. If a problem occurs with Enhanced
 framerate enabled, also try disabling that option.
 Please report remaining problems using the Bug-Report-Form on the WHDLoad
 WWW page. Include your CPU, memory configuration, WHDLoad version and
 tooltypes, and whether Enhanced framerate was enabled.

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
        https://www.whdload.de/
 or     aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and    aminet:game/patch/
